{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>If he is found.</b> In his possession — that he did not slaughter or sell." "<b>From an ox to a donkey.</b> Everything is included in double restitution, whether it has the breath of life or whether it does not have the breath of life — for it is stated in another verse: ״עַל שֶׂה עַל שַׂלְמָה עַל כָּל אֲבֵדָה … יְשַׁלֵּם שְׁנַיִם לְרֵעֵהוּ״ (Bava Kamma 62)." "<b>He shall repay double, alive.</b> And he does not repay to him dead ones, but alive or the value of live ones (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:48.910630177Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}